{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026173-through-the-gate-alternative-setting","id":1026173,"title":"Through the Gate [Alternative Setting]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-03T14:47:34-08:00","id":1026173,"title":"Through the Gate [Alternative Setting]","content":"The world was destroyed.<br /> <br /> Knowing they had only two options before them- to let the world be ruled by their ancient enemies or tear it apart, the Oracles chose the later. Calling upon magic greater then all others, they broke the world to its very foundations, moving the skies, sea, earth and sun and leaving all in ruins. From the shattered remains of the once beautiful world, they forged new worlds- five new realms governed by five great Watchtowers, worlds were truth and just would rule, and the mortals would live their life devoted to their values.. under their strict guidance, of course. Their ancient enemies, the Exrachs, were sent to a rehabilitating institute- the Labyrinth. There, they were to learn humility by themselves, their harsh character would be smooths by the life in their prison. After finishing their sentence, they may gain their place as citizens of the five worlds or in the soft and beautiful city of the Nexus. The five worlds would support each other, bringing harmony and an eternal peace through the whole multiverse..<br /> <br /> Something went wrong.<br /> <br /> The Oracles were meant to govern the Labyrinth- but they vanished without trace. Without them, the prison took life of its own- turning from a game meant to teach the Exrachs a lesson into a judge, jury and an executioner. Monsters birthed through the hatred hidden behind the nice words has hunted, butchered and murdered countless generations- and those who survived whispered the names of their tormentors each night before sleep. And after more years than anyone could count, they managed to come out through the last gate- forged by the fires of the Labyrinth and baptized with blood, the eleven Archigenitors clawed their way out- crawling on their bellies as they left paths of crimson blood. They survived- and they returned to save others from their prison. Slowly, one by one, the Exrachs escaped their prison, preparing to fight the Oracles once more.. only to find they were gone, and the Gate between the worlds locked and sealed.<br /> <br /> It took them awhile- dozens of years actually, but what are few more years for those who survived a living hell? By spending years of study and designing their spells, one of the Archigenitors took the name of the Gate (they gave up their mortal names when they named themselves as the leaders of their kind) has managed to unlock the Gate's magic and open a crack- a small one, perhaps, but enough for a well prepared person to go travel to the other worlds and investigate them. The ten other Archigenitors has divided the worlds between them, each two weaving plans to conquer one of the new worlds which were created from the bones of the old one- Arcadia, Stygia, Aether, Pandemonium and the Primal Wilds. They are going to learn those worlds, create strife and chaos behind the scenes and then- conquer them, unite them under a single rule and take their revenge against those who threw them into a prison.<br /> <br /> That is, if they are still around. Years has passed, and while the Oracles have clearly left their signs upon the separate worlds, it looks like something went wrong. Something got out of control. Relics of the past are still scattered in the form of ancient ruins, artifacts and legends- but the Oracles themselves are no where to be found. In the meanwhile, each of the worlds has developed by its own, and its people- the humans, elves and dwarves who were meant to be &quot;guided&quot; by the Oracles has waged countless wars against each other, dividing themselves into tribes and kingdoms and empires.<br /> <br /> Did the Oracles died out? If so, why? And if that's not the case- where are they? So many questions- and the answers to those questions may affect the plans of the Archigenitors in their quest for world conquest. Someone have to go through the Gate, investigate the different worlds and find those answers. Someone has to find the truth, hidden under layers of dust, war and oblivion. Someone has to travel through the thorny hedge of Arcadia, the cold rivers of Stygia, the endless storms of Aether, the madding forests of Pandemonium and the vast plains of the Primal Wilds and make sure there is no threat for the plans of the Archigenitors.<br /> <br /> And that someone is you.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> so, lately I've decided to read once more one of my favorite book series- the Death Gate Cycle- and while reading it I've thought to myself &quot;hey- doesn't it a great place to have a Mage campaign in?&quot;. While I already have more than enough other things to do, the idea of adapting certain features from the novels as an alternative Shard just were so cool I couldn't give it up. Right now I still don't have some really strong concepts about how to exactly adapt the different features from the novels and how they are going to be translated into Mage (that outcome would be some kind of hybrid- not an exact translation of the novels, but using them as a main source of inspiration), but I have some basic ideas. For example, in order to reflect the physical/spiritual divide used in the books' magic system, I've thought about giving the Exrachs (a general name for a clan of power hungry mages with affinity to the physical world) access to all of the Gross Arcana as favored and all Subtle ones as inferior, while the Oracles (a general name meant for the clan of mages dedicated into making the world a better place- that is, in the way they define as &quot;better&quot;) having Subtle as favored and Gross as inferior. I've also thought about dividing each of the Atlantean Orders as the original ruler of each world (and explore what exactly happen to them- I think they should still be around in this setting, even if in a more &quot;culturally degenerated&quot; form, to make them a playable option), while the Seers hold the Nexus. I'll post a more developed writeup for those ideas and other later.<br /> <br /> So- before we begin, does anyone have some suggestions or thoughts about the subject? Remember that powerwise, the Oracles/Exrach should be stronger then the average mages. They are demigods who had enough power to shatter one world and forge five new ones from its elements, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T16:56:22-08:00","id":1026223,"title":"","content":"The Death Gate Cycle? Never heard of it, but looks promising.<br /> <br /> So the Exarchs and Oracles are more like archmages in this setting, huh? And it looks like they're the protagonists here, in the sense that the story seems to be about them. Interesting.<br /> <hr /><br /> And, uh, I've been following your homebrews for a long time, and it kept bothering me... you consistently misspell &quot;Exarch&quot; as &quot;Exrach&quot;, and I don't think it's a typo, considering you've written dozens of posts already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T10:07:44-08:00","id":1026583,"title":"","content":"Reminds me somewhat of pre-Conflux <a href=\"http://magic.wizards.com/en/story/planes/alara\" target=\"_blank\">Alara</a> as well.<br /> <br /> So, where does the Abyss fit into all of this? Remnants from the Labyrinth?<br /> <br /> Do you have some quick descriptions of what each of the 5 worlds are like (aside from the Mage descriptions)? What some of the peoples there are like, or historical events?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T10:13:54-08:00","id":1026586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026173-through-the-gate-alternative-setting?p=1026223#post1026223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Death Gate Cycle? Never heard of it, but looks promising.<br /> <br /> So the Exarchs and Oracles are more like archmages in this setting, huh? And it looks like they're the protagonists here, in the sense that the story seems to be about them. Interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>still thinking about the exact mechanics, as I want to avoid them being too powerful- but yeah, things like 6+ Arcana and reality manipulations at high levels are a core theme of those mages. They did shattered the world once, after all- and they may do it again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <hr /><br /> And, uh, I've been following your homebrews for a long time, and it kept bothering me... you consistently misspell &quot;Exarch&quot; as &quot;Exrach&quot;, and I don't think it's a typo, considering you've written dozens of posts already. </div> </div> </div> I blame my spellchecker- it doesn't recognize the word &quot;Exarch&quot;, so I'm used to see it red- and so I keep misspelling it. I'll fix it once I'll have some time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T11:23:08-08:00","id":1026623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026173-through-the-gate-alternative-setting?p=1026583#post1026583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminds me somewhat of pre-Conflux <a href=\"http://magic.wizards.com/en/story/planes/alara\" target=\"_blank\">Alara</a> as well.<br /> <br /> So, where does the Abyss fit into all of this? Remnants from the Labyrinth?<br /> <br /> Do you have some quick descriptions of what each of the 5 worlds are like (aside from the Mage descriptions)? What some of the peoples there are like, or historical events?</div> </div> </div> </div>still thinking about how to adapt the Abyss into the setting- for now, the Labyrinth looks like the best candidate for it, and I think on making Paradox into an outcome of &quot;being scarred by the Labyrinth&quot;. Considering that the Exarchs (and those Oracles who objected shattering the worlds) all start the game by going through the Labyrinth's finale gate and get out of a world of nightmares into a place of beauty and truth, it does looks like a good parallel. Still working on the fine details, though (like, should Oracles who were not thrown into the Labyrinth suffer from Paradox).<br /> <br /> As for some quick descriptions of the five worlds, here is what I've got-<br /> <br /> <b>Arcadia</b> is, undoubtedly, the most beautiful of the five worlds. Its emerald forests cover the lands, rivers flows in endless cycles and the stars shine brightly in amazing patterns. However, this beauty hides a darker reality- the human kingdoms are found in constant infighting, with each city-state is governed by a power hungry lords. The legends speak about a mighty king who once united the different principalities under a single rule, given a divine right to do so by the gods and guided by fate weaving mystics. However, a great curse caused the king to die without heirs, tearing the kingdom asunder. While the many princes are the official rulers of their lands, all know that the true one to hold the power are the magicians, who whisper curses and blessings in an attempt to bring a new king- one ruled by them, of course. The elvish empire, on the other hand, is quit united- it far seeing mystics guide the emperor, telling him which human principality he should support and which he should betray. Their church is powerful, and their libraries contain countless prophesies up to the days when the gods walked among the mortals and tamed Arcadia'a wilderness. The dwarves live in clanish villages outside the shattered human kingdoms and the powerful elvish empire. There, they search for ancient relics left behind from the time of the ancients, selling them as weapons to the other realms. Yet, all of that covers only a small portion of Arcadia- beyond the areas tamed by the gods years ago through powerful magics, a great and thorny wilderness grows. Only the elves dare to go in there, and even they rarely do so. Stories about people getting lost in the woods an attacked by terrifying monsters have spread through the kingdoms, and those who return are transformed forever. Hidden under the earth, the dwarves sometimes find mummified bodies near the lost relics, together with astrological calendars speaking about a coming &quot;Day of Resurrection&quot;. According to their priests, the day would come soon- and then the messengers of the gods would return to guide the dwarves to rule the world.<br /> <br /> <b>Stygia</b>, on the other hand, is a cold, silent world. Its many rivers flow through countless small domains, kingdoms and villages before reaching a great abyss simply called as &quot;Oblivion&quot;. The ghosts of the dead always linger in this world, and as such the dead outnumber the living. Precious metals and gems lay depths of the earth, yet only few would dare to dig and search for them out of fearing the dark shades. Using their specialty of death magics, the humans has established a vast empire in which the dead serve the living- either as ghosts or as rotten corpses. They fight their wars, they harvest their fields, they work and preforms and spy for them. Yet the earth is barren, and barely grows enough food for the hungry mouths of the empire- forcing them to endless conquests in search for better, more fertile lands. The elves, on the other hand, fear the dead- lacking the ability to directly command them, they instead turned to ancestor worship, begging them to help them survive both the natural and human threats. Their alchemists work constantly to fertilize the land- and as such they turn into the favorite slaves of the human empire. The dwarves serve the empire as miners and crafters, harvesting the earth for metals and craft them into swords and jewellery. They are the only ones to cremate their dead, believing that by letting them linger doom would come upon the earth. For now, the empire allows that- but some start to think whether by being dead they may serve the empire better than alive. There is, however, a limit to how much the empire can spread- mysterious beings guard certain regions in Stygia, governing them through harsh rules out of forgotten duty to a power no one remembers anymore. Those who die in the realm sometimes return from their graves, as they are claimed by an ancient soul wearing a new face. The only power to stand against the empire is the Camarilla- a kingdom of the dead who yearn for the blood of the living. They have an agreement with the empire- they would not attack them, and instead the empire would supply them slaves and blood for them to feed. The agreement kept them at balance for hundreds of years- but things may change. the rumors tell about black winged birds using both the living and the dead as meat puppets, spreading war and conflict while working for some unknown agenda.<br /> <br /> well, I got to sleep now. I'll post the other three worlds tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T14:48:23-08:00","id":1026704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026173-through-the-gate-alternative-setting?p=1026623#post1026623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">still thinking about how to adapt the Abyss into the setting- for now, the Labyrinth looks like the best candidate for it, and I think on making Paradox into an outcome of &quot;being scarred by the Labyrinth&quot;. Considering that the Exarchs (and those Oracles who objected shattering the worlds) all start the game by going through the Labyrinth's finale gate and get out of a world of nightmares into a place of beauty and truth, it does looks like a good parallel. Still working on the fine details, though (like, should Oracles who were not thrown into the Labyrinth suffer from Paradox).</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would the Oracles(?) suffer Paradox? The Abyss <i>hungers</i>. And, since no Oracle was in charge of it, the Labyrinth probably mutated and considers them no different from the Exarchs it was built to torment. Since the Exarchs' escape, its Gulmoth and Acamoth wardens/creations probably see all Mages and magic use as targets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026173-through-the-gate-alternative-setting?p=1026623#post1026623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for some quick descriptions of the five worlds, here is what I've got-</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Are you going to leverage the Ruling and Inferior Arcana of each realm in their design? Like Forces manipulating magic being weak in Arcadia? Or Gravity being no match for a potent enough destiny? Spirit being Inferior in Stygia (I think) might mean there is no Animisim - spiritual entities arise from the formerly living or not at all. I think Death is Inferior in Aether, so perhaps things there never truly die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}